# Normalise line endings, so a Windows checkout stops showing whole files as
# modified when only a line or two changed.
#
# The repo already stores LF -- `core.autocrlf` happens to be on for the one
# machine this is developed on -- but nothing states it, so it survives only
# as a local setting. A second clone without that setting would commit CRLF
# and produce a diff touching every line of the file.
#
# This is deliberately declaration-only: no `git add --renormalize` is run,
# because the stored content is already LF and renormalising would churn
# every file for no change in content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
